I like the name! 

This version swaps the brightness of traditional tomatoes for deep, smoky notes and replaces the standard mozzarella with cheeses that have more "personality."

The Twist
The Sauce Base: Add 1 tsp liquid smoke or 2 tsp smoked paprika to your Bolognese while it simmers. If you’re feeling bold, deglaze the pan with 2 tbsp of Bourbon before adding the milk.
The Cheese: Use a 50/50 blend of Smoked Provolone and Smoked Gouda.

The Toppings:
Crispy bacon bits or chopped pancetta.
Caramelized onions (cooked down until jammy).
Finish: A light swirl of high-quality BBQ sauce (keep it thin!) and chopped fresh chives.

Quick How-To
The Base: Cook your Bolognese meat as usual, but lean into the smoke. Add the smoked paprika and a touch of brown sugar (just a pinch!) to the meat while browning.
The Onions: Sauté your onions separately in butter until they are dark brown and sweet.
Assembly: Spread a thin layer of the smoky meat sauce. Layer on the caramelized onions and the bacon bits.
The Cheese: Heavy on the smoked provolone/gouda blend.
Bake: Bake until the cheese has those characteristic brown "leopard spots."
The Finale: After taking it out of the oven, do a very fine "pinstripe" drizzle of BBQ sauce and hit it with the chives.
